  "content": {
    "id": "p71-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "A PIN has 4 numbers. If I forget my PIN I am allowed 3 tries to get it right.\nFind the probability that I get it within the 3 tries.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{3}{10^4}=\\dfrac{3}{10\\,000}$",
      "worked": "Each PIN position has 10 possible digits, including zero, and digits may repeat. There are $10^4=10\\,000$ possible PINs. Using three different guesses gives three acceptable outcomes.\n$$P(\\text{correct within three tries})=\\frac{3}{10^4}=\\frac{3}{10\\,000}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
